From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] xdgshellwindow: resize back while another size is pending
Description:
 XdgSurfaceWindow::moveResizeInternal() compares the requested size with the
 size the client committed last. If they are equal, it only updates the frame
 geometry and sends no configure event. When a configure event with another
 size is still pending, the client acknowledges that event afterwards and
 commits its size, so the request back to the committed size is lost.
 .
 This happens when a window is resized twice before the client commits:
 the on-screen keyboard opens (configure with the reduced height) and closes
 again, or its geometry changes while it is going away, before the client
 has answered. The window then keeps the reduced height with no keyboard on
 screen.
 .
 Send a configure event as well when the last pending configure event asks
 for a different size than the request. The same idea is proposed upstream
 in merge request 9814 (not merged as of this date); this is an own, smaller
 variant that only looks at the last pending event.
Forwarded: no (upstream proposal: https://invent.kde.org/plasma/kwin/-/merge_requests/9814)
Bug: https://bugs.kde.org/show_bug.cgi?id=459136
License: GPL-2.0-or-later (as the patched file)
Last-Update: 2026-11-24
---
--- a/src/xdgshellwindow.cpp
+++ b/src/xdgshellwindow.cpp
@@ -271,7 +271,19 @@
         const QSizeF roundedRequestedClientSize = surface()->snappedSize(requestedClientSize);
 
         const QSizeF roundedClientSize = surface()->snappedSize(clientSize());
-        if (roundedRequestedClientSize == roundedClientSize) {
+
+        // The client ends up with the size of the last configure event it acknowledges. If that
+        // event asks for another size, a request back to the committed size needs a configure event
+        // of its own, otherwise it would be overridden by the stale event on the next commit.
+        bool pendingResize = false;
+        if (!m_configureEvents.isEmpty()) {
+            const RectF pendingBounds = m_configureEvents.constLast()->bounds;
+            if (!pendingBounds.isEmpty()) {
+                pendingResize = snapToPixels(pendingBounds.size(), nextTargetScale()) != requestedFrameSize;
+            }
+        }
+
+        if (roundedRequestedClientSize == roundedClientSize && !pendingResize) {
             const RectF snappedRect = RectF(rect.topLeft(), nextClientSizeToFrameSize(snapToPixels(roundedClientSize, nextTargetScale())));
             updateGeometry(m_nextGravity.apply(snappedRect, rect));
         } else {
